  [94m]8;id=1uda2i6;http://localhost:56841/?key=36bce6b695ddb1c676a32d0265a33c24d4a31f454a787957c332108c95050e74\http://localhost:56841/?key=36bce6b695ddb1c676a32d0265a33c24d4a31f454a787957c332108c95050e74[39m]8;;\. The sketches use quite a
  lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.

  The page shows three layouts. Each has the 9 event-type checkboxes, the date range and a "Showing X of 48 events"
  count.

  - [1mA:[0m a filter panel above the table that's always open.
  - [1mB:[0m a "Filter" button that opens a popover, with the active filters shown as removable tags.
  - [1mC:[0m a sidebar to the left of the table.

  I recommend A. People will use both filters together every time (failed sign-ins and security changes in one week), so
  hiding them behind a button just adds a click. A also needs no popover focus handling, and it reflows to 320px by
  stacking. C takes about a quarter of the table's width, and the table has six columns.

  Tell me which one you prefer here in the terminal. You can also click a layout in the browser to select it.

  The companion stores its files in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m at the repo root, and [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m doesn't list that folder yet. I won't
  commit anything in it. You may want to add it to [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m.

